      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chauncey%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village sits where Sunday Creek meets the Hocking River, a spot that has made flooding a long‑standing issue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chauncey%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1932 striking miners sabotaged a New York Coal Company track near Mine #25, prompting National Guard deployment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chauncey%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 19th‑century Athens County Infirmary just outside Chauncey is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
